# clasp pushes everything under rootDir by default. These belong to the
# repository, not to the Apps Script project: the harness is Node and the editor
# would reject it, and the rest is documentation and clasp's own config.
#
# outreach/ is the other Apps Script project entirely — a standalone one owned by
# the sending account. Without this line clasp would push the sender's six files
# into the bound project, where they would run as the sheet owner. That is the
# one identity the whole design exists to keep away from GmailApp.
#
# Both the bare and the **/ form are listed because clasp has matched only one of
# them depending on the version.
outreach/**
**/outreach/**
harness.js
**/harness.js
README.md
**/README.md
.claspignore
**/.claspignore
.clasp.json
**/.clasp.json
.clasp.json.example
**/.clasp.json.example
# clasp pull materialises Apps Script files as .js; the source of truth here is .gs.
*.js
**/*.js
